# _rl_jobs.inc - Jobs and the runners' road (Umsetzung 14, Phase 3 sections 5 and 6).
# Shared by every madam, told in a narrator's voice. Plain ASCII only.
{1000}{}{Work that needs doing outside.}
{1001}{}{(Outside these walls there is always somebody to pay, somebody to lean on and somebody to rob.)}
{1002}{}{Pay Tyler to look the other way. ($100 a week)}
{1003}{}{Stop paying Tyler.}
{1004}{}{Put a Downtown cop on the payroll. ($80 a week)}
{1005}{}{Take the cop off the payroll.}
{1006}{}{Send for the gravedigger from Golgotha. ($300)}
{1007}{}{Donate to McClure's peace fund for Gecko. ($1000)}
{1008}{}{Lean on the small stalls outside. Protection money.}
{1009}{}{Leave the stalls alone.}
{1010}{}{Intercept a rival's delivery.}
{1011}{}{Steal a rival's books.}
{1012}{}{Sell the stolen books back to their owner. ($300)}
{1013}{}{Pay for a sick room in the Den. ($500)}
{1014}{}{Make a donation to the NCR Rangers. ($1000)}

{1020}{}{(Tyler takes the first hundred without counting it. His boys stop loitering in front of the door.)}
{1021}{}{(Tyler shrugs. He was never your friend. Now he isn't paid to pretend.)}
{1022}{}{(Officer Grady pockets the envelope. From now on he writes his reports about other streets.)}
{1023}{}{(The cop takes the news badly. He knows the address now, and he isn't paid to forget it.)}
{1024}{}{(Two men with a handcart come at night. By morning there are no bodies, and nobody asks where they went.)}
{1025}{}{(McClure accepts the donation with a speech about the common good. He remembers your name, and so does the council.)}
{1026}{}{(A few broken jars, one broken finger. After that the stall owners pay on time and don't look anyone in the eye.)}
{1027}{}{(The stall owners pay. The next morning Sheriff Marion stands in front of the Slag with his thumbs in his belt. He doesn't say anything. He doesn't have to.)}
{1028}{}{(The stall owners keep their money. None of them thanks you.)}
{1029}{}{(The crates never arrive. Somebody else's customers wait in vain this week, and some of them end up at your door.)}
{1030}{}{(The ledger is thick and badly bound. Names, debts, payments to people who are supposed to be honest. Worth a lot to the right reader.)}
{1031}{}{(The owner pays without haggling and never mentions it again. Neither do you.)}
{1032}{}{(A room with clean sheets and a man who knows what he's doing with a needle. The Den talks about it for weeks.)}
{1033}{}{(The Rangers take the money and give you a receipt. On the next patrol they walk past your door without stopping.)}

# The runners' road through Broken Hills
{1040}{}{The runners' road through Broken Hills.}
{1041}{}{(The runners carry the week's money from Redding, Vault City and the NCR to New Reno. The road runs through Broken Hills, and Broken Hills belongs to Sheriff Marcus. He takes no money. He watches.)}
{1042}{}{(Broken Hills is a relay station now. Marcus' people know your runners by name. Half as many go missing.)}
{1043}{}{(Marcus' deputies ride with your runners as far as the next town. Almost nobody goes missing anymore.)}
{1044}{}{(Broken Hills is closed to your runners. They take the long way around, lose a week and lose more money.)}
{1045}{}{(Nobody talks to Marcus without going to Broken Hills first.)}
{1046}{}{[Speech] Talk to Marcus. Tell him plainly what the houses are.}
{1047}{}{Offer Marcus money to look the other way.}
{1048}{}{Show Marcus how your houses treat their people.}
{1049}{}{(Marcus listens for a long time. "I don't like your business. I like liars less. Your runners can rest here. If one of them steals, I'll hang him myself.")}
{1050}{}{("You want to pay me to look away? I never look away. That's why humans and mutants still live side by side here." Marcus doesn't forget the offer.)}
{1051}{}{(Marcus reads the ledgers, talks to two of your girls, then to a third. "Fair shares. Doctors. Nobody locked in." He sends two deputies with every runner.)}
